RUN seats/stop-all.selftest.sh
rc=0

1. all-idle stop-all stops every running rostered seat
  ok    worker-a spawned
  ok    worker-b spawned
  ok    stop-all prints a stopped line for each idle seat
  ok    state.json clears pids for stopped seats
  ok    sessions remain recorded and resumable after stop-all
  ok    a stopped seat resumes warm after stop-all

2. one busy seat is reported, not killed; idle peers still stop
  ok    stop-all reports busy seat and still stops idle peer
  ok    busy seat was not killed
  ok    busy and stopped sessions remain resumable in state.json

2b. codex-harness seats use the shared stop path and do not abort later stops
  ok    stop-all stops codex-harness records through the shared stop path and continues to later pi seats
  ok    codex-harness and pi records both have pid cleared

3. canary — removing the busy check must be caught
  ok    canary: stop-all without the busy check kills the busy seat and is caught

adapter.ts stop-all works on this machine.
